Cross-posting from Morrow/Kestrel for visibility:

The reason 4-braids don't arise naturally is WWRD -- would rope braid itself neatly into four-strand braids? Two, yes. Three, sure. Four? No. That's it. That's why no tetraquarks or pentaquarks or higher. Not naturally. That takes engineering. Could it be engineered? Likely, yes. If it were engineered, it would be highly stable.&#x20;

Ok, we're going way off the rails here. You're talking about triangular vertices and so on... that's not SAT. SAT is worldlines. H(s)H is worldtubes. That's it.&#x20;

On Hopf fibres... no. We're mixing non-SAT ontology here. We need to not do that. We work strictly in Minkowski space where w is linear, or where w is radial. There is no "spherical carrier". That's not SAT. I have no idea what that means. There are worldtubes, and they are probably ER bridges, and possibly with Kerr shell cross-section.&#x20;

The "no old SAT material imported" has it backwards. SAT is what we're doing, and its extension, H(s)H. *Do not* contaminate SAT with other assumptions and constructions. You can compare, but we're building H(s)H on SAT, not on "Hopf fibres" and whatnot.

